# Security

Never commit secrets. Use `.env.local` locally, Vercel env vars for the app, and GitHub Actions secrets for migrations.

Never put service-role keys in frontend code or `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variables.

Never trust the browser for payment status, bid validity, quota availability, exchange balances, order fills, signature completion, or admin permissions.

Never edit immutable financial or position ledgers in place. Corrections use adjustment or reversal entries.

Use database transactions for concurrent money and position operations.

Payment and webhook handling must be idempotent.

API keys stored for exchanges must be trade-only, with no withdrawal permission.
